	/// Definition: The typical rate at which clients leave a case manager over about the past year, shown as the middle value across the selected case managers and areas.
	/// - Weeks: rolling 52 weeks
	/// - Fortnights: rolling 25 fortnights
	/// - Months: rolling 12 months
	/// For analysis: Not used on any page. Not for analysis; the Fortnights branch adds the rates instead of taking the median. Use the median of the snapshot Client Rolling Churn Rate column.
	measure ClientMedianRollingTurnover =
			SWITCH(
			    TRUE(),
			    SELECTEDVALUE(PeriodParam[MonthWeekParam Fields]) = "'DimDate'[Start of Month]", MEDIAN(FactCMMonthlySnapshot[Client Rolling 12M Churn Rate]),
			    SELECTEDVALUE(PeriodParam[MonthWeekParam Fields]) = "'DimDate'[Fortnight Start Date]", SUM(FactCMFortnightlySnapshot[Client Rolling 25Fn Churn Rate]),
